Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): load and apply editable gamerules in Java options

Java 26.3 waits for a GAME_RULE_VALUES response before showing its in-world rules screen. Return the matching rules received from Bedrock and translate validated edits into Bedrock command requests. Omit rules whose behavior or value type differs between editions, and respect the Bedrock editable flag.

Map Java's locator_bar to Bedrock's playerWaypoints rule. Bedrock 1.26.60.5
game rule registration 0x14070a550 has no locatorBar rule. It registers
playerWaypoints as an int rule with default 1 that accepts values below 2,
and lambda 0x140729570 migrates a stored legacy locatorbar value (false to
0, true or absent to 1). The old locatorbar mapping never matched a
current server rule. Translate 0 and 1 to Java false and true, skip other
values, and send Java edits as 0 or 1.

